error[E0277]: `Box<Widget>` can't cross the WeaveFFI C ABI
 --> tests/ui/fail_box_param.rs:8:16
  |
8 | pub fn take(w: Box<Widget>) {
  |                ^^^ not a WeaveFFI value type
  |
  = help: the trait `weaveffi::rt::types::FfiType<Tag>` is not implemented for `Box<Widget>`
  = note: a value is a scalar (`i32`, `f64`, `bool`, `usize`, ...), `char`, `String`, `Vec<T>`, `Option<T>`, a `HashMap` or `BTreeMap`, a `#[weaveffi::record]`, a `#[weaveffi::enumeration]`, a `#[weaveffi::custom]` type, or a `#[weaveffi::interface]` as `Arc<T>`
  = note: a parameter may also be borrowed (`&str`, `&[T]`, `&T`), and only a whole return may be a `weaveffi::Iter<T>`
help: the trait `weaveffi::rt::types::FfiType<Tag>` is implemented for `Arc<Widget>`
 --> tests/ui/fail_box_param.rs:4:1
  |
4 | #[weaveffi::interface]
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = note: this error originates in the macro `::weaveffi::__weaveffi_interface` which comes from the expansion of the attribute macro `weaveffi::interface` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

